farmland-atlas/texas/mclennan-county"],["ARC or PLC in McLennan County","/arc-plc/texas/mclennan-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the McLennan County record runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids July to August came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them. In 2025 the middle of the grids saw February to March at 57% of normal and June to July at 222%. In 2026 so far, February to March came in at 36% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 13331 had its driest year in 1954 at 44%.</p>"}
